# System files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
# Working diffs left at the root by a person or an agent. Two have landed here
# already (#1869, and a reviewer's scratch-diff.patch during HARNESS-120).
/*.patch
/*.diff

# Sensitive data
*.secret
*.dec
# Key material must never reach the commit path (ADR-028). Root-anchored on
# purpose: sensitive/dr/.gitignore deliberately UN-ignores its own escrow
# artefacts, so a broad `*.key` would reach into a rule that is load-bearing.
# Two empty ones (`.nan.key`, `nan.key`) were left here while testing the
# doctor's secrets checks; nothing in this repo tracks a `*.key`.
/*.key
/.*.key
.venv/
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.development
.env.staging

# Machine-local shell overrides (IDEAS-001) — non-sensitive, per-machine
.zshrc.local
.bashrc.local
.tmux.conf.local

# Cross-machine path resolution (ADR-025). The per-machine override lives at
# ~/.config/dotfiles/machine.json (outside the repo); the generated path files
# are rendered into ~/.dotfiles. Both are ignored here defensively so a stray
# `dotf env generate --output .` or a copied machine.json never gets committed.
# The committed reference is machine.json.example, not machine.json.
/machine.json
/paths.sh
/paths.ps1

# Development tools
node_modules/
*.log

# Go build artifacts — the CLI installs to ~/.local/bin via install.sh; a local
# `go build` in cli/ leaves an untracked binary that must never be committed.
/cli/dotf
/cli/dotf.exe
# …and the same binary when `go build -o dotf.exe ./cmd/dotf` is run from the
# repo root instead of cli/. CI writes its binary to a temp dir (ci.yml), so a
# root-level one is always a local build; the dirty check behind `dotf worktree
# done`, `sweep` and `list` already treats it as disposable. Nothing tracked
# in this repo has a .exe extension.
/*.exe
# `go test -coverprofile` writes here. It was tracked from #1404 until #1408
# untracked it: a profile is a measurement of one run on one machine, so it
# conflicts on every branch that touches cli/ and its diff says nothing.
/cli/coverage.out

# IDE/Editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-*

# Test reports dropped at the root by an ad-hoc run (`testResults.xml`). No
# workflow or script in this repo writes that name any more, so it can only
# arrive here by hand; a report is a measurement of one run, like coverage.out.
# Nothing tracked has an .xml extension.
/*.xml

# Cache directories
.cache/
.npm/
.yarn/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
.astro/
.worktrees/

# AI
# .claude/ is deliberately NOT ignored wholesale: CLAUDE.md is this repo's
# project instructions (binding, reviewable, restorable) and belongs in git.
# Only the genuinely machine-local entries are excluded.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/plans/
.gemini/
.ai/
AGY.md
CLAUDE.md
# ...except this repo's own project instructions, which are binding and must be
# versioned, reviewable and restorable. The rule above still catches a deployed
# CLAUDE.md landing at the repo root.
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
.aider*
.antigravitycli/
.antigravitycli.bak/

# Added by ggshield
.cache_ggshield

# Adversarial-review machine logs. Not artifacts: `dotf spec review` writes the
# reviewer's raw event stream beside the verdict, and it is large and churning
# while a review runs.
#
# `**` rather than `*` because `*` does not cross a `/`, so `specs/*/` stopped
# matching the moment `spec archive` renamed a spec into `specs/archive/<id>/` —
# and archiving is exactly when the file is at its largest. HARNESS-072's was
# 552 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, so the archive commit could not have
# been pushed at all (#998).
specs/**/review-transcript.jsonl
specs/**/review-transcript.jsonl.stderr
specs/**/review-second-transcript.jsonl
specs/**/review-second-transcript.jsonl.stderr
